    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The equation $\\sin 2x \\sin 3x = \\cos 2x \\cos 3x$ can be rewritten as $\\sin (2x + 3x) = \\cos (2x + 3x)$, which further simplifies to $\\sin 5x = \\cos 5x$.\n\nSince $\\sin y = \\cos y$ when $\\tan y = 1$, the angle $x$ that satisfies this equation is $5x = 45^\\circ$ (as every 45° interval in this equation will have the same answer). Therefore, the smallest positive angle $x$ that satisfies $\\sin 2x \\sin 3x = \\cos 2x \\cos 3x$ is \\boxed{20^\\circ}.",
